+// Era_Row — one era row (Story 6.1, eras.json — the S6 Era FSM's data, GDD M4).
+// The row is the AUTHORITATIVE per-era declaration: which packet classes are
+// ACTIVE (the roster — "streaming becomes available" is a roster change), which
+// demand.json era holds the era's demand signature (demand_era — the demand
+// CONTENT stays single-source in demand.json, ODN-5; this cross-ref binds it),
+// and the infrastructure unlock table (node types + pipe tiers the era makes
+// available). All cross-refs are resolved to indices at load (fail-fast on
+// unknown ids — ODN-5), and the load enforces the era_introduced exact-
+// equality invariant (the roster + unlock tables must equal the per-item
+// era_introduced-derived sets) so the two data sources can never drift.
+// Sim values are integers only (ODN-10). Stored at index era-1 (padded, like
+// demand.eras — array, map-free, ODN-10).
+Era_Row :: struct {
+	era:          u8,
+	id:           string,
+	display_name: string,
+	// the active packet-class roster, resolved to packet_types indices at load
+	// (fail-fast on an unknown id).
+	packet_classes: [dynamic]u16,
+	// demand.json era index carrying this era's demand signature (the demand
+	// content — entries + set-pieces — is single-source in demand.json; this
+	// pins the binding + validates the row exists).
+	demand_era:   u8,
