+# switches: era 3's demand (email res→res + streaming content_host→res) spawns
+# from the NEXT tick. The T1 pins the era-advanced state; the captures prove
+# the traffic visibly changes (pre-advance: email circles only; post-advance:
+# streaming triangles join the map — "the internet evolves, new traffic
+# appears"). The base draw (res→router→host over standard) gives the era-2
+# email spec a sink set (fixture qos adds two more residentials).
+seed 20261
+run 60000ms
+era 2
+fixture qos
+at 0ms draw 0 1 standard
+at 0ms draw 1 2 standard
+at 25000ms advance 3
+capture at 10000ms
+capture at 55000ms
